  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Defense has obligated $260B in contracts in FY2026 to date. That total covers 2,218,119 awards with an average award size of $117K, and obligations are down 47.2% year over year. FY2026 to date spending sits below recent full fiscal years, which ranged from $387B in FY21 to $492B in FY25. The largest NAICS categories so far are Aircraft Manufacturing at $32.9B, Engineering Services at $23.9B, and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $23.8B. Health-related spending also appears in the top categories, with Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $11.9B and several large medical supply and contractor entries among the top vendors. Top vendors include multiple entries for LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10B and $9.2B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.5B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $6.3B. These figures are partial, fiscal year to date totals, and reflect contract obligations rather than completed payments or outlays.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 to date contracting compare with recent years?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations total $260B, which is lower than the recent full-year totals of $387B in FY21, $414B in FY22, $457B in FY23, $446B in FY24, and $492B in FY25. Obligations are down 47.2% year over year. The current award count is 2,218,119 and the average award size is $117K, showing the year to date picture of volume and scale."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What spending areas and vendors dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Top spending categories are led by Aircraft Manufacturing at $32.9B, followed by Engineering Services at $23.9B and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $23.8B. Among top vendors, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION appears at $10B and $9.2B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION is $8.5B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY is $6.3B, with other large vendors including THE BOEING COMPANY, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP, HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC, AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP, and RTX CORPORATION."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Defense spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense has obligated $260B in contracts in FY2026 to date. That total covers 2,218,119 awards with an average award size of $117K, and obligations are down 47.2% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Defense buy?",
      "a": "Defense buys a mix of platforms, services, and support led by Aircraft Manufacturing ($32.9B), Engineering Services ($23.9B), and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing ($23.8B). Other top categories include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences ($18B), Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers ($11.9B), and Ship Building and Repairing ($11.6B)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Defense's largest contractors?",
      "a": "Defense's largest contractors in FY2026 to date include LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $10B and $9.2B, ELECTRIC BOAT CORPORATION at $8.5B, and RAYTHEON COMPANY at $6.3B. Other top vendors are THE BOEING COMPANY ($5.9B and $4.3B entries), TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP ($4.6B), HUMANA GOVERNMENT BUSINESS INC ($4.6B), AMERISOURCEBERGEN DRUG CORP ($4.5B), and RTX CORPORATION ($3.7B)."
